## 1. esplora — the two A16 defaults, paths confirmed live

GET https://blockstream.info/api/block-height/800000 -> 200, 64 B, no trailing newline
GET https://mempool.space/api/block-height/800000    -> 200, 64 B, no trailing newline
  both: 00000000000000000002a7c4c1e48d76c5a37902165a270156b7a8d72728a054

GET https://blockstream.info/api/block/<hash>/header -> 200, 160 B (80 bytes, lowercase hex)
GET https://mempool.space/api/block/<hash>/header    -> 200, 160 B
  BYTE-IDENTICAL between the two services (diff clean). This is the property
  A16's byte-identity rule rests on, and it holds because an esplora header is
  a fixed-width 80-byte object with no encoding freedom — NOT because two
  endpoints generally agree byte-for-byte (A17 is the counter-case, §2).

GET .../api/block-height/99999999 -> 404, 15 B, body exactly `Block not found`
  on BOTH services, byte-identical, no trailing newline. This is the agreed
  -absence case that becomes `OnlineBlockResult::NoSuchBlock` (D56 rule O7).

Files:
